✓ Stack1 grows from left (index 0 → size-1)
✓ Stack2 grows from right (index size-1 → 0)
✓ Overflow when top1 + 1 == top2 (stacks meet)
✓ Underflow: top1 == -1 (stack1 empty), top2 == size (stack2 empty)
✓ Both stacks share single array efficiently
✓ No wasted space until array is completely full
✓ All operations O(1) time, O(n) space for single array

